X: 1
T: The Grave Itself a Garden Is 
T: (also known as Upon the Sixth Day of the Week)
C: Words: Christopher Wordsworth, 1862, alt.
C: Music and Setting: 'Belmont' William Gardiner, 1812.
C: copyright: public domain.  This score is a part of the Open Hymnal Project, 2026 Revision.
S: Music and Lyrics source: "The New Hymnal (Episcopal)", 1916 Hymn 166.  This hymn is essentially verses 6, 8-12 of the original.  
S: The original was intended as an Easter hymn (and could certainly still be used as such)
M: 3/4 % time signature
L: 1/4 % default length
